<article class="env-theorem" id="03V3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03V3">Theorem <span data-tag="03V3">64.20.4</span>.</a> Let $X/k$ be as above, let $\Lambda $ be a finite ring with $\# \Lambda \in k^*$ and $K\in D_{ctf}(X, \Lambda )$. Then $R\Gamma _ c(X_{\bar k}, K)\in D_{perf}(\Lambda )$ and </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \sum _{x\in X(k)}\text{Tr}\left(\pi _ x |_{K_{\bar x}}\right) = \text{Tr}\left(\pi _ X^* |_{R\Gamma _ c(X_{\bar k}, K )}\right).  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that we have already proved this (REFERENCE) when $\dim X \leq 1$. The general case follows easily from that case together with the proper base change theorem. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>